<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Western Front (World War I)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1914–1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Western Front was the main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, a line of trenches running about 700 kilometres from the Belgian coast to the Swiss border after the German advance was halted at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marne">Marne</a> in 1914. Battles such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verdun">Verdun</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somme-river">Somme</a> and Passchendaele cost millions of casualties, until Allied offensives in 1918 forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> to seek an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/western-front-world-war-i.jpg" alt="Western Front (World War I)" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: At_close_grips2.jpg: H.D. Gridwood The Battle of the Somme film image2.jpg: Geoffrey Malins Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R05... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Front_(World_War_I)_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
